For me the fun in playing Nethack is in the playing.  When you
were a kid exploring the neighborhood as a game, was there a
contest for who could visit every block first?  No, I just rode my
bike around for the fun of it.  Same as in Nethack.

As a pacifist you already have almost unlimited chances to die
in the game.  Get the Candellabra.  Find the vibrating square.
Kill Rodney.  Then go escape from the dungeon with abunch of
artifacts and leave out the rest of your life in wealth.  And end up
way up there on the high score list.  Sure, any score that
includes an ascension beats any score that doesn't.  But that
doesn't mean that getting a high score sucks.



